You hit the nail on the head. This is a classic race condition caused by asynchronous threading.
When the user clicks "Submit" for a bulk upload, your backend spins up a background thread to build the batch and instantly returns the batchId to React so the UI doesn't freeze. However, React is so fast that by the time the user clicks "Confirm Schedule" on the success screen, the background thread is still inserting the 10,000 line items and hasn't gotten around to creating the VOUCHER_POSTING master record yet!
Your intuition is exactly right: we need to create the master VOUCHER_POSTING record *synchronously* before returning the batchId to the frontend. Then, the background thread can take its time inserting the child rows into VOUCHER_POSTING_DATA.
Here is how to split the logic to perfectly fix this issue.
### 1. Make Master Record Creation Synchronous
Find your createBatchFromCacheAsync method in VoucherRequestServiceImpl.java and replace it with this. This grabs the row count from Redis instantly, saves the master record, and *then* fires the background thread.
```java
    @Override
    @Transactional
    public String createBatchFromCacheAsync(String requestId, String commonRemarks, String creatorId, Integer creatorRole, String vid) {
        String lockKey = "LOCK_REQ_" + requestId;
        Boolean acquired;

        try {
            acquired = redisTemplate.opsForValue().setIfAbsent(lockKey, new byte[0], 60, TimeUnit.MINUTES);
        } catch (DataAccessException e) {
            log.error("REDIS_LOCK_FAIL | ReqID: {} | Status: Connection to lock service failed", requestId);
            throw new CustomExceptions.DatabaseOperationException("Distributed lock service unavailable", e);
        }

        if (Boolean.FALSE.equals(acquired)) {
            log.warn("CONCURRENCY_LOCKED | ReqID: {} | Status: Processing already in progress", requestId);
            throw new CustomExceptions.ConcurrencyLockException("Batch creation is already in progress for this Request ID.");
        }

        try {
            String batchId = sequenceService.getNextBatchId(); 
            String journalPrefix = sequenceService.getNextJournalIdPrefix(); 

            // ✨ 1. Fetch total rows from Redis synchronously (takes 1 millisecond)
            byte[] metaBytes = redisTemplate.opsForValue().get("DATA_META_" + requestId);
            long totalRows = 0;
            if (metaBytes != null) {
                try {
                    Map<String, Object> meta = objectMapper.readValue(metaBytes, new TypeReference<>() {});
                    totalRows = ((Number) meta.get("totalRows")).longValue();
                } catch (Exception ignored) {}
            }

            // ✨ 2. Create the Master Record synchronously BEFORE returning to the UI
            String workflowCode = jdbcTemplate.queryForObject("SELECT WORKFLOW_CODE FROM WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS WHERE ALLOWED_ROLE_ID = ? AND WORKFLOW_ORDER = 1 FETCH FIRST 1 ROWS ONLY", String.class, creatorRole);
            Long firstApproverWorkflowId = jdbcTemplate.queryForObject("SELECT WORKFLOW_ID FROM WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS WHERE WORKFLOW_CODE = ? AND WORKFLOW_ORDER = 2", Long.class, workflowCode);

            VoucherPosting posting = new VoucherPosting();
            posting.setBatchId(batchId);
            posting.setVidFk(vid);
            posting.setCommonBatchRemarks(commonRemarks);
            posting.setCreatorRole(creatorRole);
            posting.setCreatedBy(creatorId);
            posting.setWorkflowCode(workflowCode); // Fixed mapping
            posting.setPendingAt(firstApproverWorkflowId);
            posting.setBatchStatus("P");
            posting.setIS_EXECUTION_SCHEDULED("NO");
            posting.setScheduledTime(null);
            posting.setIsScheduleOverride("NO");
            posting.setRecordsCount(totalRows);
            voucherPostingRepository.save(posting);

            if (vid != null && !vid.isEmpty()) updateVidStatus(vid, VoucherStatus.USED);
            logWorkflowAction(batchId, vid, "Submitted", creatorId, commonRemarks, null);

            progressService.sendProgress(batchId, creatorId, 0, "PROCESSING", "Initializing Batch Creation...");

            // ✨ 3. Pass down to async thread to handle the heavy line-item insertion
            self.executeAsyncBatchCreation(batchId, journalPrefix, requestId, commonRemarks, creatorId, creatorRole, vid);

            // Now guaranteed to exist in the database for the schedule API!
            return batchId; 
        }
        catch (DataAccessException e) {
            redisTemplate.delete(lockKey);
            log.error("SEQUENCE_GEN_FAIL | ReqID: {} | Status: Failed to generate sequence", requestId);
            throw new CustomExceptions.DatabaseOperationException("Failed to generate Batch ID sequence", e);
        }
    }

```
